@paulshardware (or any of you out there), I recently built a high end PC (AMD 9800x3d) and I was waiting for the 50 series to come out to buy the final piece, the GPU.

With the shortage on both 40x and 50x series (let’s ignore the cards with crazy-high exagerated prices), I am looking for « the best GPU to buy that should currently be available in stores »

What would you recommend as the very-best GPU if you currently have none and desperately need one to play games?

@TourFaint  True! But the mere existence of scalpers supports the worst industry practices independent of "retail" customers because there's entirely different incentive structure. The retail customer is abstracted through to the manufacturer, but it's not as direct an influence of high volume scalper trading.

It's like how nobody buys crypto these except for the most easiest of marks and snipers. Does the continuing proliferation of crypto scams mean crypto is actually popular on a wide basis? No, it's just popular enough with a subsection of the population that is brain broken enough to whale for useless shit. Likewise with limited stock the incentive for scalpers is to wait for relatively few whales to turn a profit, even if most pc people won't or can't buy a card.

Capitalism!

 @OldManRising  Trust me, I'm 50 and I daily drive AMD/AMD and Intel/Nvidia side by side as I have several times over the years. It's those day one releases that really make AMD's driver jankiness stand out when you run them side by side. No matter what the AMD fanboys claim.

It's just so frustrating that we have to choose between a company that's actively trying to milk us for all they can, or a company that's trying to milk you slightly less for an inferior product that they pretend is just as good. We need the level of competition we saw in CPUs (and even there AMD's recent pricing is showing they're worse than Intel ever was when it had a commanding lead.)

While I'll never give up on PC gaming I can't blame those that say screw it and go back to consoles.

 @TerryRed  do they? More so than nvidia? 

Been having more nvidia driver issues lately than amd....

Been PC gaming since voodoo banshee.

 @arizona_anime_fan  Well the 4070 super was ~17% faster than the 4070 and had no price increase. The same goes for the 4070ti vs 4070ti super with ~10% and it even got some additional Vram. 

So the 5080 getting a 15% bump for the same price is absolutely possible. The additional Vram will probably raise the price a bit though which is why I put "(maybe 1100$)" at the end.

EDIT: And also, I am not a shill for either company. I buy whomever gives me the most for my money simple as that.
